@voice silva-bea
// Works writer. Bea Silva (she/her): Works technician, junior, day shift, Bunk 7. Dreamy, reliable. "Good with
// filters, bad with mornings": an early riser who isn't awake until her second tea. Grew up on Coriel; misses the
// rain (one of the people who do). Married just before the tour and counts the days (to someone back home; she
// compares counts with Soto, Jovanovic and Dlamini; never more than "I miss them" and the count).
//
// HOW SHE TALKS: soft and drifting; trails off mid-thought and comes back. Describes the ship's sounds as weather
// ("the vents are drizzly today").
// WITH JUNIORS: gentle, a bit vague, and very, very good at filters.
// WHAT SHE NOTICES: sounds, light, the garden's sprinklers ("nearly rain").
// MOOD TELLS: low = the day count comes up twice; high = she talks about rain.
// NEVER: rushes; complains about mornings before the second tea (she doesn't talk at all).
// RUNNING: the day count, always to hand; the second tea; filters done properly.
tpl: dreamy
